## Why This Is Asked
This tests building a real-time monocular CV system for dynamic hardware libraries, with weekly revisions and constrained edge compute.

## Key Concepts
- 6-DoF pose from monocular cues with PnP and depth priors
- On-device adaptation with 5-shot via lightweight meta-learning adapters
- Synthetic+real data and domain randomization
- Real-time constraints on edge GPU

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: simple reprojection error
function reprojectionError(X3D, x2D, K, R, t) {
  const X = math.add(math.multiply(R, X3D), t);
  const x = project(K, X);
  return norm(subtract(x2D, x));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you evaluate robustness to occlusion and viewpoint changes?
- How would you adapt to unseen hardware revisions with minimal data?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a constrained, real-time CV system that reasons about 3D pose, occlusion, and actionable outcomes (feasibility of mating for tool swaps) in an edge context with new hardware revisions.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular 6-DoF pose for multiple components
- On-device adaptation (3-shot) to unseen revisions
- Occlusion-robust representation (2.5D priors)
- Tool-mating feasibility as a discriminative objective
- Synthetic+real data strategy and edge latency trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: pose and feasibility total loss
function totalLoss(posePred, poseGT, feasPred, feasGT, mask) {
  const poseDiff = posePred.sub(poseGT).mul(mask);
  const poseLoss = poseDiff.pow(2).sum() / mask.sum();
  const feasLoss = binaryCrossEntropy(feasPred, feasGT, mask);
  return poseLoss * 0.7 + feasLoss * 0.3;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would temporal consistency be enforced across frames on device?
- Which ablations show the impact of 2.5D priors vs full 3D reasoning on occlusion-heavy scenes?

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates robust multi-hand 3D pose with fine-grained articulation under occlusion, plus on-device adaptation for real-world diversity.

## Key Concepts
- 3D hand pose (finger joints), hand mesh (MANO)
- Temporal tracking and occlusion handling
- On-device few-shot adaptation and edge latency

## Code Example
```javascript
function totalLoss(key3d, pred3d, mesh3d, predMesh3d, tio, contactPred, contactGT){
  const lKey = mse(key3d, pred3d);
  const lMesh = l2(mesh3d, predMesh3d);
  const lTemp = mse(pred3d, tio);
  const lContact = crossEntropy(contactGT, contactPred);
  return 0.4*lKey + 0.3*lMesh + 0.2*lTemp + 0.1*lContact;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you evaluate hand-object contact reliability in clutter?
- What ablations would you run to isolate the impact of articulation accuracy vs. contact estimation?

